      "dom_id": "question-364163",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Maya and Leon get paid for painting houses. The ratio of Maya's reward to Leon's reward is $3:4.$ \nDuring a particular week, Leon received $$806.$ By rounding Leon's earnings to the nearest hundred, approximate the amount of money that Maya received.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the amount of money that Leon received:\n\n$$\n$806⟶$800\n$$\n\nThe ratio of Maya's earnings to Leon's earnings is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents Maya's earnings  and the denominator represents Leon's earnings.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $800$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $200$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 200}{4\\times 200}=\\frac{600}{800}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Maya received approximately $$600.$",
