      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-364172\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">5.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/555#2284\">Finding a Value by Approximating Ratios</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"364172\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The number of laptops and tablets in store A is shown in the following table:</p>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" font-size=\"inherit\" rules=\"all\" style=\"border: 1px solid black\" width=\"300px\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\" width=\"50%\"> Laptops </th>\n<th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"text-align:center\" width=\"50%\"> Tablets </th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"45\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>72</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"46\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>38</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>In store B there are approximately <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"47\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> laptops. The ratio of the number of laptops to the number of tablets in both stores is the same. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of tablets in store B.</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:03 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:14</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>",
